BERTopic dedicates an entire topic to "junk" or "noise". This topic is not part of the $K$ topics listed, but is an extra $K(+1)$th topic.

The results in @table:bertbasenoise show that the number of documents classified as noise almost always is at least 50%. Overall, the @d2 embeddings have a somewhat higher noise percentage but both cases are very high. These results indicate the need to investigate other BERTopic variations that decrease the high amounts of noise documents.


