=== ETM <res:etm>

The ETM exclusively utilized @d2 to generate its embeddings. Instead of the dynamic embeddings used for CTM and BERTopic, ETM uses static embeddings that must be generated every run, instead of precomputed. 

ETM has a fixed vocabulary size. One of its strengths compared to LDA is that it should be able to handle a larger vocabulary. For this reason the results in @table:etm are compared based on the number of topics generated aswell as two different vocabulary sizes, 2000 words and 6000 word.


