Observing the coherence score displayed in @fig:etmcoher, the ETM appears to score about the same across most topics, but slightly higher at $K = 20$. Utilizing a 2000 words vocabulary scores higher than the 6000 word vocabulary for all number of topics. The highest score of 0.083 was achieved for $K = 20$ topics.

The diversity is shown as a bar chart in @fig:etmdiv and for both the vocabulary sizes it shows a clear decrees as the number of topics increase. The 6000 word vocabulary scores higher in diversity in all cases except for $K = 10$ topics where it is surpassed by the 2000 word vocabulary. 10 topics is also where ETM has its overall highest diversity.

The runtime visualized in @fig:etmtime differs between the two vocabulary sizes. The smaller vocabulary stays at 420-440 seconds runtime for all topics while the the larger vocabulary causes the model to sometimes take over 600 seconds to finish. The smaller vocabulary was also more stable in this regard as the larger vocabulary varied between 550-650 depending on the number of topics generated. the 2000 vocabulary version was indeed much more stable but by observing the values in @table:etm they somewhat increase with the number of topics.

