== Summary of model results <res:sum>

This section aims to showcase how the different models compare to each other. These results will guide the answer to the research question described in @intr:prbl. Since the models performed differently under different circumstances, this section focuses on comparing them at their best. this means that if a model performed well for a certain number of topics but poorly for another, the better result is considered. 

Topic coherence is considered the most important metric and is thus the metric that decides which models are included in this section. This is because coherence is deemed to be the metric that best represents the human interpretation of "good" topics, as described in @bg:mtr. The models and their specific configuration is listed in @table:bestmodels

All models only contribute with one version of themselves except for BERTopic. BERTopic have two additional variations, BERTopic-@hdbscan presented in @res:hdscan and BERTopic-Reassign presented in @res:reass. This is because their usefulness for reducing noise must be weighted against their performance on the other metrics.


