The coherence score of the models is plotted in @fig:sumcoher. The bar chart shows the base BERTopic in the lead followed by BERTopic-Reassign. after a drop in coherence CTM is the third best performing. Changing the @hdbscan parameters of BERTopic made it drop down to a forth place. The fith best performing model was the LDA which still scored very similarly to CTM. After another visible drop in score the ETM appears last.

Worth of note is also that most models with the exception of the BERTopic variants scored the best when generating a smaller number of topics, $K <= 30$.


The same models as presented in @fig:sumcoher but instead with their diversity displayed is shown as a bar chart in @fig:sumdiv. The chart shows that the CTM scored the best in diversity followed by the LDA and the base BERTopic model. These were then followed by the two BERTopic variants. ETM scored the worst in diversity.

A summary of the metrics can be seen in @fig:sumcvd, where diversity is plotted against coherence so that the tradeoff can be clearly seen.


